<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Holowczyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1708">1708</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Holowczyn · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Holowczyn was fought in 1708 in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII of Sweden</a> defeated a Russian army in what was one of his last major victories. The campaign continued into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and ended in disaster at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Poltava</a> the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-holowczyn.jpg" alt="Battle of Holowczyn" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: B. Adlerfeld · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holowczyn_1708_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Charles XII (r. 1697–1718) represented the apogee of personal Swedish generalship: a commander of extraordinary tactical skill whose victories at Narva (1700) and <b>Holowczyn</b> (1708) against numerically superior opponents rank among the finest tactical performances of the early eighteenth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire · Military</a></li></ul></section>
